  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "$3÷\\frac{6}{7}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{6}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{6}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{3}{1}÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6} & =\\frac{3}{6}\\times \\frac{7}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
